A||||39||Ken Wittlief||101 Wurstest Christmas gifts :cO||||11||
Z||000000||Ken Wittlief||12-18-2001||08:51 PM||||For me there is no greater mystery or puzzle than trying to find a perfect gift for the special someone in your life. I dont think I have ever come close to giving a perfect gift, but I have come up with some real stinkers. And I have seen other people I know pull some Christmas fisacos too.<P> So I bet with your help we can come up with 101 things to NOT buy for christmas presents:<P>1. Lottery tickets. Lets think this through. You spend $5 or $10 on lottery tickets for a present - there are two possibilities:<BR> <BR> A. The tickets are loser - the recipiant finds out in 60seconds or less that he has no gift.<P> B. The ticket is worth millions of dollars - you just gave someone a million dollars or more for christmas - do you think they will share it with you?! Wouldnt it have been better to win the money yourself, and then decided how much YOU want to share?!<P>2. Engagement ring - if you are going to marry someone you are suppose to buy them a ring anyway - so isnt this like getting out of buying a christmas present?! And if you are going to spring it as a surprise then what if she says no?! What a sucky christmas party that is going to be!<P> I know a guy who not only proposed to someone on christmas, but he invited friends, family and a minister over on christmas day for a surprize wedding! Talk about putting someone on the spot, and setting yourself up for a major embarassment :cO When you ask someone to marry you, isnt the other person suppose to feel completely free and unpressured to decided yes or no?<P>3. Consumables: anything that gets used as part of something else - like batteries, blank tapes, blank CDs, glue sticks... These are things that people are going to buy anyway, and all it lets them do is keep using something they already have.<P>4. Gift certificates. Isnt this almost like giving someone money, but also saying "I know if I give you cash you will spend it on something I wont approve of, so you HAVE to goto this place to pick out your gift!'<P>5. Any book that you think the person NEEDS to read - like a self help book or a religous book - if its something you want them to read then give it to them at some other time, not as a gift - chances are they dont want to read it so you end up giving them something they dont really want.<P>6. an expensive musical instrument or one that takes time and training to learn to play - if they didnt specifically ask for it you have just laid a major investment of personal time and energy on them - chances are it will end up in a closet within the week.<P>7. Something that is for YOUR interests. Every couple has stuff they do together, but its really one person who is interested in it, and the other is only participating to spend time together - like if the guy likes to go fishing, and the girl tags along sometimes - then fishing is HIS thing - dont buy her a new fishing pole for christmas if thats the case - you have to recognise what things the other person is really interested in, and which things they are only doing to spend time with you.<P>8.||||reg||11
Z||000001||fogglethorpe||12-18-2001||10:04 PM||||Other bad gifts:<P>Cat food<BR>Barbra Streisand CD<BR>Plastic Gandhi statuette<BR>"Skin Rash of the Month Club" lifetime membership<BR>||||reg||13
Z||000002||Cooter||12-18-2001||10:13 PM||||Re: Number 7<BR>I always buy my wife something that I like, that way after the "new" wears off, I get a present too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tina||12-18-2001||11:01 PM||||Appliances.....or anything else that requires a powercord and is used primarly to do household chores with.<P>Defininate NO NO...in some cases you actually score <B>Minus</B>points with stuff like that.<P>Tina   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Tina (edited 12-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jaygee79||12-19-2001||01:41 AM||||any health-related place (unless specifically asked for).  that'll getcha a guaranteed 6 months on the couch.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Haagster||12-19-2001||06:14 AM||||Got my wife a dustpan to go with the broom that I got her last Christmas  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>*** Sorry.  Couldn't resist stealing an old Diceman joke ***||||reg||6
Z||000006||AusFiero||12-19-2001||06:21 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tina:<BR><B>Appliances.....or anything else that requires a powercord and is used primarly to do household chores with.<P>Defininate NO NO...in some cases you actually score [b]Minus</B>points with stuff like that.<P>Tina    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>[This message has been edited by Tina (edited 12-18-2001).][/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>My wife thinks they are definate no nos too. Why?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>More things not to get for christmas. <P>1. A voucher from a new girlfriend or boyfriend for a  free visit to an STD clinic.<BR>2. A Mustang  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> (Maybe we should put that up top)<BR>3. A casket and/or burial plot.<BR>4. Tickets to a Britney Spears concert. (ok Roger might like it)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>5. A lifetime membership card to AA.<BR>6. A visit from the authorities. (that would have to suck, getting locked up Christmas day.)<BR>7. A Mustang. (well I know I said that but 2 would be worse than 1)hehe<BR>8. An iron duke to replace your V6.<BR>9. A 2.8 to replace your newly installed 3.8 or V8.<BR>10. A pine tree air freshener for your Fiero.<P><P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/auschristmas.gif">        <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroBUZZ||12-19-2001||09:19 AM||||Definately not a great idea to ask the wife if she'd like to go to the laser place to get her moustache done.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||13
Z||000008||Ken Wittlief||12-19-2001||09:53 AM||||-Candles<P>- a case of bags for the vacuum cleaner<P>- Nothing! have you ever been in the situation where money is tight, or you are saving up for a down payment on a house, and your spouse says these magic words "Dont buy me anything for Christmas this year"<P> IN THE NAME OF GOD DONT LISTEN TO HER!!! She is being noble - sell your spleen for money if you have to but buy her SOMETHING!||||reg||11
Z||000009||Ken Wittlief||12-19-2001||01:54 PM||||- any kind of article or story you clip out of a newspaper or magazine, and then put into a nice frame - no matter how much you think the recipiant will 'love this' :c0||||reg||11
